#    This creates a coarse-grain outer loop (jo) that we can parallelize
#    and keeps accesses to A[i, j] within relatively small contiguous blocks.
p = divide_loop(p, u_j, TILE_J, ("jo", "ji"), tail="guard")

# 5) Parallelize the outer j-tile loop for each fixed i.
#    For a given i, different j iterations of the U update are independent:
#      - Each iteration writes a distinct A[i, j] location.
#      - All reads A[i, k] and A[k, j] come from rows < i or L entries
#        computed before entering the U loop.
#    Thus, parallelizing over jo is safe and maps to an OpenMP parallel-for
#    in the generated C code.
lu_i = p.find_loop("i")
jo = lu_i.body().find_loop("jo")
p = parallelize_loop(p, jo)

